------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE 180-DEGREE = COGNATE CLAIM, CHECKED AGAINST ENGLISH
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  If 180-degree rotation encodes the voiced/unvoiced cognate relation, then
  Dorabella's 13 adjacent mirror pairs are 13 adjacent cognate phoneme pairs.

    adjacent cognate pairs in the phoneme corpus : 18,048 of 3,999,999
    rate                                         : 0.451%
    expected in 86 adjacencies                   : 0.39
    observed mirror pairs                        : 13

    z of 13 against that expectation             : +20.3

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE CONSONANT-SKELETON VARIANT, WHICH THE ARITHMETIC FORCES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Reading (b) -- cognates as DISTINCT symbols sitting at 180 degrees -- needs
  all 16 cognate consonants present as separate symbols. With the 8 unpaired
  consonants that is 24 already, leaving nothing for vowels. So reading (b)
  forces a consonant-only cipher. That is Pitman-consistent: Pitman outlines
  are consonant skeletons with vowels as optional dots, and Dorabella has dots.
  Checked on its own terms:

    consonant skeleton length      : 2,420,039 of 4,000,000 phonemes  (60.5%)
    adjacent cognate pairs         : 50,204 of 2,420,038  = 2.075%
    expected in 86 adjacencies     : 1.78
    observed mirror pairs          : 13     z = +8.5
    share needed to expect 13      : 15.12%  (section 11.2)

    87 consonants ~ 144 phonemes ~ 44 words
